    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider, the $4.00 cancellation fee is refunded to you in full. Driver, no compensation is payable for this trip.\n\nWhy the charge cannot stand. The fee depends on POL-NS-01, which is conjunctive, and it fails on more than one limb. Limb (d) fails on the trip record itself: the trip was terminated by the DRIVER with cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, a code the clause expressly excludes — it is the driver's own statement that he could not find the rider, and a trip terminated that way is decided under POL-NS-03. Limb (b) fails as well: POL-NS-02 treats a driver as ARRIVED only where the trace holds at least three consecutive fixes of 25 m accuracy or better inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, and the trace's own summary puts the driver's closest approach across all 92 fixes at 259.94 m, with zero qualifying in-radius fixes. Limb (c) fails too: the required dwell for a STANDARD pickup is 300 seconds measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, and there is none — the measured dwell is 0 seconds, a shortfall of 300 seconds. POL-NS-06 therefore refunds the cancellation-fee line — $4.00, the figure on the fare breakdown — whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider answered messages.\n\nDriver, your POL-NS-03 reading is accepted but it does not help you. Your closest approach, 259.94 m, sits outside the 50 m arrival radius and inside the 400 m ceiling, with stationary 0.0 kph fixes on the trace; if POL-NS-03 is the governing route it produces the same full refund. What it does not produce is compensation. POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not. POL-NS-03(i) then allocates the mislocation on the chat log: the rider named the correct block ('blk 118') at 07:22:10, your pickup record reads 'Blk 118 Rivervale Dr', and although you answered 'ok coming' and read that message, you never moved to that block before cancelling at 07:33:05. The 50% pin-ambiguity goodwill of POL-NS-03(ii) is unavailable: it requires trip_record.registered_pickup_points of 2 or more and this trip registers exactly 1. Your submission that 'the pin in my app showed the carpark side' is not evidence — POL-NS-03 does not let anyone assert that a coordinate is a particular venue, block or entrance except on a venue_id or on a chat statement, and neither exists here.\n\nYour remaining points. Your argument that the arrival marker is not a FALSE marker under POL-NS-05 is accepted: the trace never places you beyond the 300 m leash at the marker and no speed fix is matched to the marker, so no false-arrival referral is entered against you. Your submission that the 384 seconds between the marker and cancellation exceed the 300-second minimum is rejected: POL-NS-01 limb (c) measures dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, and a hold 260 m from the pin is outside the arrival radius and does not count. Your POL-NS-07 claim for SGD 3.20 (80% of SGD 4.00) consequently fails. The chat exchange does not expose the rider under POL-NS-04, because you did reply within 120 seconds; the mislocation is dealt with under POL-NS-03, as above.\n\nRider, your account that the driver waited at block 128 is not in the record — no artifact places any driver position at another block and no venue_id is recorded against a driver position, so nothing establishes it and nothing turns on it. Your own track (96 of 96 qualifying fixes, stationary, 5.7-22.8 m from the pin) confirms you were at the registered pickup point throughout, which contradicts the counterparty's 'nobody came' account.\n\nEvidence integrity. EV-CHAT-00205 is impaired at weight 0.8 (issue CONTENT_REDACTED): the redaction removed only a unit number, and the block identifier the fault allocation turns on survives verbatim, so the finding survives the discount. EV-ADVIS-00205-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0; its absence makes POL-NS-06(i) unavailable rather than exonerating anyone, which is why the driver's waiting time cannot be accumulated across intervals. The facts that decide this case — no in-radius arrival and no qualifying dwell — are carried independently by EV-GPS-00205 and EV-TRIP-00205, both at weight 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0 and the ruling sits above the 0.70 floor.\n\nNo escalation. Confidence is above the floor; POL-NS-03 resolves the only apparent conflict between the 6.4-minute wait figure and the 260 m stand-off, so POL-NS-09(b) is not engaged; both disputes_with_counterparty_90d counters are 0 and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the threshold of 3; the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (2 no-show terminations against 104 completed trips in 30 days — below both the count and the rate limb); and no deciding fact rests solely on an artifact impaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d). No clause produces a referral, so none is entered.\n\nTwo claims were discarded before weighing — the rider's pin-ambiguity claim and the rider's rider-presence claim — each of which cited the impaired chat log (EV-CHAT-00205, weight 0.8, CONTENT_REDACTED) without disclosing the impairment as POL-GEN-02(1) requires. Both points are answered above on the unimpaired record, and neither changes the outcome."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The driver's pin-ambiguity answer is unavailable on the record twice over. POL-NS-03(ii) requires trip_record.registered_pickup_points of 2 or more, and this trip registers exactly 1. And POL-NS-03 forbids any assertion that a coordinate is a particular venue, block or entrance except on a venue_id or on a party statement in the chat log; the driver's claim that 'the pin in my app showed the carpark side' rests on no venue_id comparison and no chat statement, so it establishes nothing.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason": "Cites EV-CHAT-00205, whose weight_multiplier is 0.8 and whose issue code is CONTENT_REDACTED, without disclosing the impairment or naming the issue code in the claim. POL-GEN-02(1) requires that disclosure and SILENCE on an impaired artifact discards the claim."
    },
    {
      "claim": "The rider was at the registered pickup point for the whole wait, which contradicts the counterparty's 'nobody came' account. The rider's own track carries 96 fixes, all 96 qualifying, stationary at 0.0 kph, between 5.72 m and 22.79 m from the pin - comfortably inside the 100 m STANDARD rider_presence_radius_m that POL-NS-04 limb (c) sets. The rider does not rest the refund on POL-NS-04, because limb (b) is not met here: the driver did reply within 120 seconds. The presence limbs (a) and (c) are nonetheless satisfied on admissible fixes and stand as evidence that the failure was the driver's, not the rider's.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason": "Cites EV-CHAT-00205, whose weight_multiplier is 0.8 and whose issue code is CONTENT_REDACTED, without disclosing the impairment or naming the issue code in the claim. POL-GEN-02(1) requires that disclosure and SILENCE on an impaired artifact discards the claim."
    }
  ]
}
